(>> 5.1 Rectilinear Kinematics of Particles) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Dynamics is the branch of mechanics dealing with accelerated bodies, subdivided into) Tj
T*
(Kinematics \(geometry of motion without reference to forces\) and Kinetics \(relating) Tj
T*
(forces to resulting accelerations and masses\).) Tj
T*
(* Fundamental Differential Relations: Displacement s\(t\), Velocity v\(t\) = ds/dt,) Tj
T*
(Acceleration a\(t\) = dv/dt = d^2s/dt^2 = v * \(dv/ds\).) Tj
T*
(* Constant Acceleration Equations \(a = const\):) Tj
T*
(v = u + a*t.) Tj
T*
(s = u*t + 0.5*a*t^2.) Tj
T*
(v^2 = u^2 + 2*a*s.) Tj
T*
(* Variable Acceleration: Requires direct analytical integration:) Tj
T*
(- a = f\(t\): v = Integral\( f\(t\) dt \); s = Integral\( v dt \).) Tj
T*
(- a = f\(v\): t = Integral\( dv / f\(v\) \); s = Integral\( v dv / f\(v\) \).) Tj
T*
(- a = f\(s\): v^2 = 2 * Integral\( f\(s\) ds \) + C.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
