(Problem Context: A civil engineering piling hammer moves along a vertical guide with) Tj
T*
(variable acceleration given by a\(t\) = \(12*t - 3*t^2\) m/s^2, where t is in seconds. At t) Tj
T*
(= 0, displacement s\(0\) = 0 m and initial downward velocity v\(0\) = 4.0 m/s. Calculate:) Tj
T*
(\(1\) Maximum velocity achieved, \(2\) Velocity at t = 3 s, \(3\) Total displacement at t = 3) Tj
T*
(s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Derive velocity function v\(t\):) Tj
T*
(v\(t\) = v\(0\) + Integral_0^t a\(tau\) dtau = 4 + Integral_0^t \(12*tau - 3*tau^2\) dtau.) Tj
T*
(v\(t\) = 4 + [ 6*t^2 - t^3 ] m/s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Maximum Velocity Condition:) Tj
T*
(Maximum velocity occurs when dv/dt = a\(t\) = 0 => 12*t - 3*t^2 = 0 => 3*t*\(4 - t\) = 0 =>) Tj
T*
(t = 4.0 s.) Tj
T*
(v_max = v\(4\) = 4 + 6*\(4\)^2 - \(4\)^3 = 4 + 96 - 64 = 36.0 m/s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Velocity at t = 3.0 s:) Tj
T*
(v\(3\) = 4 + 6*\(3\)^2 - \(3\)^3 = 4 + 54 - 27 = 31.0 m/s.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Derive displacement function s\(t\) and evaluate at t = 3.0 s:) Tj
T*
(s\(t\) = Integral_0^t v\(tau\) dtau = Integral_0^t \(4 + 6*tau^2 - tau^3\) dtau = [ 4*t +) Tj
T*
(2*t^3 - 0.25*t^4 ].) Tj
T*
(s\(3\) = 4*\(3\) + 2*\(3\)^3 - 0.25*\(3\)^4 = 12 + 54 - 0.25*\(81\) = 66 - 20.25 = 45.75 m.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Maximum velocity = 36.0 m/s; Velocity at t=3s = 31.0 m/s; Displacement at) Tj
T*
(t=3s = 45.75 m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
