(Problem Context: Block A \(mass m_A = 20 kg\) rests on a 30-degree inclined plane) Tj
T*
(\(coefficient of kinetic friction mu_k = 0.20\) and is connected by a light inextensible) Tj
T*
(cord passing over a frictionless pulley to a hanging Block B \(mass m_B = 30 kg\). Using) Tj
T*
(D'Alembert's principle, calculate the acceleration a of the system and cable tension T.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Establish Kinematic Relations and Dynamic Equilibrium:) Tj
T*
(Assuming Block B descends vertically with acceleration a, Block A moves UP the incline) Tj
T*
(with identical acceleration a.) Tj
T*
(For Block A on incline:) Tj
T*
(Normal reaction: N_A = m_A * g * cos\(30\) = 20 * 9.81 * 0.8660 = 169.91 N.) Tj
T*
(Friction force \(opposing motion down incline\): F_k = mu_k * N_A = 0.20 * 169.91 = 33.98) Tj
T*
(N.) Tj
T*
(Downhill gravity component = m_A * g * sin\(30\) = 20 * 9.81 * 0.50 = 98.10 N.) Tj
T*
(Reversed Inertia Force = m_A * a = 20 * a \(directed down incline\).) Tj
T*
(Dynamic equilibrium along incline: T - 98.10 - 33.98 - 20*a = 0 => T - 20*a = 132.08 N.) Tj
T*
(\(Equation 1\)) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Dynamic Equilibrium for Hanging Block B:) Tj
T*
(Downside gravity force = m_B * g = 30 * 9.81 = 294.30 N.) Tj
T*
(Cable tension T \(upward\); Reversed Inertia Force m_B * a \(upward\):) Tj
T*
(Dynamic equilibrium vertically: 294.30 - T - 30*a = 0 => T + 30*a = 294.30 N. \(Equation) Tj
T*
(2\)) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Solve Simultaneous Equations for a and T:) Tj
T*
