(Problem Context: A pile driver hammer A \(mass m_A = 1200 kg\) falling vertically hits a) Tj
T*
(stationary concrete pile cap B \(mass m_B = 800 kg\) with impact velocity v_A1 = 8.0 m/s) Tj
T*
(\(v_B1 = 0\). The coefficient of restitution is e = 0.40. Calculate: \(1\) Post-impact) Tj
T*
(velocities v_A2 and v_B2, \(2\) Total loss of kinetic energy during impact.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Conservation of Linear Momentum:) Tj
T*
(m_A * v_A1 + m_B * v_B1 = m_A * v_A2 + m_B * v_B2.) Tj
T*
(\(1200 * 8.0\) + \(800 * 0\) = 1200 * v_A2 + 800 * v_B2.) Tj
T*
(9600 = 1200 * v_A2 + 800 * v_B2 => 12 * v_A2 + 8 * v_B2 = 96 => 3 * v_A2 + 2 * v_B2 =) Tj
T*
(24. \(Equation 1\)) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Coefficient of Restitution Equation:) Tj
T*
(e = \(v_B2 - v_A2\) / \(v_A1 - v_B1\) => 0.40 = \(v_B2 - v_A2\) / \(8.0 - 0\).) Tj
T*
(v_B2 - v_A2 = 0.40 * 8.0 = 3.2 m/s => v_B2 = v_A2 + 3.2. \(Equation 2\)) Tj
T*
