(>> 5.7 University Review & Examination Questions) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Q1: State D'Alembert's Principle and explain how it simplifies the solution of) Tj
T*
(dynamic engineering problems.) Tj
T*
(Answer: D'Alembert's Principle states that a dynamic system in motion under applied) Tj
T*
(external forces can be brought into formal static equilibrium by adding a fictitious) Tj
T*
(inertia force equal to the product of the mass and acceleration vector acting in the) Tj
T*
(direction opposite to acceleration \(F_inertia = - m * a\). Thus, Sigma F + \(- m * a\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(Its primary significance is that all established analytical tools of statics \(free-body) Tj
T*
(diagrams, resolving orthogonal forces, moment equilibrium about instantaneous centers\)) Tj
T*
(can be directly applied to dynamic systems without solving coupled second-order) Tj
T*
(differential equations.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Derive the Work-Energy Theorem for a particle moving along a general curved) Tj
T*
(spatial path.) Tj
T*
(Answer: Consider a particle of mass m moving along path s under resultant force F.) Tj
T*
(Tangential Newton's second law states: F_t = m * a_t = m * v * \(dv/ds\). Multiplying both) Tj
T*
(sides by differential displacement ds: F_t * ds = m * v * dv. Integrating both sides) Tj
T*
(from initial state \(s1, v1\) to final state \(s2, v2\): Integral_s1^s2 \(F_t ds\) =) Tj
T*
(Integral_v1^v2 \(m * v dv\). The left side is the total external work done U_1-2. The) Tj
T*
(right side evaluates to: [ 0.5 * m * v^2 ]_v1^v2 = 0.5 * m * v2^2 - 0.5 * m * v1^2 =) Tj
T*
(Delta KE. Hence, Sigma U_1-2 = Delta KE.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
