T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Variable acceleration requires direct calculus integration: v = Integral a dt, s =) Tj
T*
(Integral v dt.) Tj
T*
(* Normal acceleration a_n = v^2/rho directs toward curve center; tangential a_t =) Tj
T*
(dv/dt changes speed.) Tj
T*
(* D'Alembert's principle adds reversed inertia force \(-m*a\) to apply static) Tj
T*
(equilibrium equations.) Tj
T*
